{title: You Are the Man}
{subtitle: 2 Samuel 11:1–27; 12:1–25}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In spring the kings march out to [F]war
David [Bb]stayed in Jerusa[F]lem
He walked the [Eb]roof of the king's house
[F]Saw a woman bathing there [Gm]
She was Bathsheba daughter of E[F]liam
Wife of [Bb]Uriah the Hittite
[F]David sent messengers for [Eb]her
And [F]slept with her that [Gm]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are the man Nathan [Bb]said
As the [Eb]Lord lives the [F]man must [Gm]die
Repays four [Eb]times for the [F]little ewe
Who [Gm]had no pity [F]in his [Eb]eye
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]David sent word to [F]Joab
Send me [Bb]Uriah the Hittite
Uri[F]ah slept at the gate of the [Eb]house
He did not go to his [F]own door
[Gm]David wrote a letter in the [F]morning
[Bb]Put him where the fighting is fier[F]cest
[Eb]Pull back so he is struck [F]down
[Eb]Joab obeyed the [F]king's com[Gm]mand
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]Bathsheba heard her husband [F]died
She [Bb]mourned for him in [F]grief
When the [Eb]mourning was over
David [F]sent for her a[Gm]gain
She became his wife and bore a [F]son
But the child [Bb]did not live
Nathan spoke [F]of [Eb]disaster rising
From [F]within the king's own [Eb]house
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are the man [F]Nathan said
[Gm]As the Lord lives the man must die
Re[Bb]pays four times for [Eb]the little ewe
[F]Who had no [Gm]pity in his [Eb]eye
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The sword [F]will never de[Gm]part
From your house [F]because you [Eb]despised me
I gave you your master's [Bb]house
[Eb]And if it was [F]too little [Gm]I would add more
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You are the man Nat[Bb]han [Eb]said
You are the [F]man
{end_of_verse}

